{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"plan","namespace":"","artifact_type":"","name":"Pb31107bf"},"owner_reference":"#3268","content":"{\"plan_id\":\"Pb31107bf\",\"feature\":\"groom-swarm-dispatch-contract\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\",\"description\":\"\",\"goal\":\"Make the dh subagent dispatch contract internally consistent: every agent with backlog MCP access self-fetches item content by reference, orchestrator-facing rules for dispatch-prompt scope and anti-speculation live in dispatch-contract, and the groom/close workflow docs stop instructing orchestrators to paste content that is addressable by item_ref.\",\"context\":\"Documentation / prompt-contract fix for #3268. No executable code, no tests, no CI changes.\\n\\n**Authoritative spec**: `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__artifact_read(item_id=3268, artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\")` \\u2014 path `plan/architect-groom-swarm-dispatch-contract.md`. Every task below names the spec section (\\u00a71\\u2013\\u00a76) carrying the exact replacement text. Read the spec section before editing; do not re-derive wording from the item description.\\n\\n**Problem context**: `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__artifact_read(item_id=3268, artifact_type=\\\"feature-context\\\")` \\u2014 WHY, risks R1\\u2013R8, open questions Q1\\u2013Q9.\\n\\n**Scope correction recorded in spec \\u00a70 (read first)**: the original 4-file brief becomes 5 files. The orchestrator-facing rules (dispatch-prompt scope + no speculative conclusions) go to `dispatch-contract/SKILL.md`, because `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md:265-267` states dispatch behaviour belongs in the `dispatch-contract` skill \\\"and nowhere else\\\". Only the agent-facing self-fetch rule stays in `subagent-contract/SKILL.md`. Do not move either rule into the other file.\\n\\n**Files edited (one task each, all disjoint \\u2014 safe to run in parallel)**:\\n1. `plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md` (T1)\\n2. `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/swarm.md` (T2)\\n3. `plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md` (T3)\\n4. `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch-contract/SKILL.md` (T4)\\n5. `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/close/start.md` (T5)\\n\\n**Files that must NOT be edited** (already-compliant reference pattern, verified read-only by T6): `agents/impact-analyst.md`, `agents/classifier.md`, `agents/alignment-analyst.md`, `agents/rtica-assessor.md`, `agents/fact-checker.md`.\\n\\n**`fact-checker` is the accepted exception, not a defect.** Its pasted `CLAIM` / `SOURCE_FILE` / `PRIMARY_SOURCE` / `VERIFICATION_METHOD` / `FALSIFICATION_CRITERIA` block is genuinely per-run dynamic content that no `item_ref` lookup retrieves. No task may rewrite it or extend the self-fetch rule over it.\\n\\n**Deliberately out of scope (follow-ups, do not touch)**: `groom/error.md`, `groom-drift.md`, `quick/start.md`, `work/post-planning.md`, `add-new-feature`/`implement-feature` specialist dispatches, the `task-worker.md` identity mismatch, feature-context Q6 (`fact-checker` PRIMARY_SOURCE anchoring surface), and feature-context Q7/R5 (mechanical guard for the anti-speculation rule \\u2014 no new test code in this plan).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Context Manifest\\n\\n### Execution Strategy\\n\\nThe plan has two dependency phases:\\n\\n**Phase 1 (parallel)**: T1, T3, T4, T5 run concurrently. Each edits one file with no cross-task dependencies.\\n- **T1** (`backlog-item-groomer.md`): Adds Step 0.0 self-fetch rule to the groomer's Input contract. Fixes acceptance criterion AC1 (backlog_view grep count becomes nonzero).\\n- **T3** (`subagent-contract/SKILL.md`): Adds orchestrator-agnostic `<dispatch_input>` section teaching agents with backlog MCP to self-fetch. Fixes AC3 (dispatch_input tag count becomes 2).\\n- **T4** (`dispatch-contract/SKILL.md`): Adds orchestrator-facing `<dispatch_prompt_scope>` scope rule. Fixes AC4 (dispatch_prompt_scope tag count becomes 2).\\n- **T5** (`close/start.md`): Collapses Step 5.6 items 4\\u20135 into a single spawn directive handing the reference to the verification agent. Fixes AC5 (grep 'Parse each' count becomes 0).\\n\\n**Phase 2 (sequential, depends on Phase 1)**: T2 runs after T1 and T4 complete.\\n- **T2** (`swarm.md`): Replaces prose and diagram to hand groom-swarm teammates `item_ref` instead of pasted content. Depends on T1's Step 0.0 and T4's `<dispatch_prompt_scope>` for the cross-references. Fixes AC2 (grep 'item details' count becomes 0).\\n\\n**Verification gate (sequential, depends on all implementation tasks)**: T6 runs after T1\\u2013T5 complete.\\n- **T6**: Read-only audit confirming the four reference-pattern self-fetching agents remain unchanged and T3's exception clause covers the fifth (fact-checker). Produces a report. Fixes AC6 (five agent files diff is 0 lines).\\n\\n### What \\\"Done\\\" Looks Like\\n\\nAll six acceptance criteria pass:\\n\\n| AC | File | Criterion | Current \\u2192 Target |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| **AC1** | backlog-item-groomer.md | groomer calls backlog_view | 0 \\u2192 nonzero |\\n| **AC2** | swarm.md | 'item details' phrasing removed | 2 \\u2192 0 |\\n| **AC3** | subagent-contract/SKILL.md | `<dispatch_input>` tags present | 0 \\u2192 2 |\\n| **AC4** | dispatch-contract/SKILL.md | `<dispatch_prompt_scope>` tags present | 0 \\u2192 2 |\\n| **AC5** | close/start.md | orchestrator no longer parses criteria | 1 \\u2192 0 |\\n| **AC6** | Five reference agent files | no changes by any task | 0 \\u2192 0 |\\n\\nWhen all ACs pass, the contract is internally consistent:\\n- **Agent side** (T3): Every agent with backlog access is instructed to self-fetch, with an exception for per-run-generated content.\\n- **Orchestrator side** (T4): Every orchestrator is forbidden from pasting addressable content and pre-formed verdicts into dispatch prompts.\\n- **Implementation** (T1, T5): Two workflow consumers (`backlog-item-groomer`, verification in `close`) fetch their own item content instead of awaiting pasted text.\\n- **Documentation** (T2): The groom-swarm sequence diagram and prose agree with each other and with the agents' own self-fetch contract.\\n- **Integrity** (T6): The five reference-pattern agents that established this pattern are unchanged, confirming the fix does not regress already-compliant code.\\n\\n### Cross-Task Integration Points\\n\\n**T1 \\u2192 T2**: T2's prose cites `backlog-item-groomer.md:Step 0.0` (created by T1) as proof that the groomer will fetch. T2's verification step 5 checks this reference resolves.\\n\\n**T3 \\u2190 T2**: T2 explicitly names `dh:dispatch-contract` as the source for orchestrator scope limits. T3's counterpart `<dispatch_input>` rule (agent side) is mentioned in T4, not T2, to keep the audiences separated.\\n\\n**T4 \\u2192 T2**: T2's prose cites `dh:dispatch-contract` (created by T4) as the scope authority. T2's verification step 5 checks this reference resolves.\\n\\n**T5 (solo)**: Standalone close-workflow fix. No forward or backward dependencies; its Item 5/6 renumbering is local.\\n\\n**T6 (read-only gate)**: Depends on T1\\u2013T5 by reading their outputs to audit consistency, not by being written-to by any prior task. If T6 detects a CONFLICT (e.g., T3's exception clause ambiguity), the conflict is reported against the rule wording, and T3 would need re-execution.\\n\\n### End-to-End Flow\\n\\nThe fix resolves the two observed symptoms in the item:\\n\\n1. **Symptom**: Groom-swarm teammates (`impact-analyst`, `classifier`, etc.) are dispatched with pasted item content despite their own files saying they self-fetch.\\n   - **Fix**: T1 adds Step 0.0 to groomer; T3 documents the agent-side rule; T2 rewrites swarm.md to hand references.\\n   - **Verification**: T6 confirms no agent files were modified and the new T3 rule doesn't conflict with them.\\n\\n2. **Symptom**: Close workflow's verification step re-types acceptance criteria into the dispatch prompt instead of handing the reference to an agent that has backlog MCP access.\\n   - **Fix**: T5 collapses Step 5.6 to hand the reference, instructing the agent to fetch and parse itself.\\n   - **Verification**: AC5 confirms the orchestrator-parse language is gone.\\n\\nBoth halves are balanced by the orchestrator-facing rule (T4), which forbids speculative conclusions and pre-formed verdicts from traveling in dispatch prompts. The three rules (T1 Step 0.0 agent fetch, T3 agent-side `<dispatch_input>`, T4 orchestrator `<dispatch_prompt_scope>`) form a complete contract.\\n\\n### Known Constraints and Deferrals\\n\\n- **Spec \\u00a70 scope correction is non-negotiable**: dispatch behaviour must land in `dispatch-contract/SKILL.md` per AGENTS.md:265-267. Do not relocate the T4 section into `subagent-contract`.\\n- **Fact-checker exception is not a defect**: Its pasted content is per-run-produced (claim text to verify, sources to check). T3 must preserve this exception; T6 verifies it is not a contradiction.\\n- **No test/CI changes**: The anti-speculation rule (T4) is a property of runtime prompt text that no test at rest can observe. Feature-context Q7/R5 is a follow-up.\\n- **Five reference-pattern agents are read-only**: T6 is the audit; no task may modify them. They are the proof that the pattern works.\\n\\n### Rollback and Conflict Recovery\\n\\nIf T6 detects a conflict:\\n- **Dangling reference** (T2 cites T1/T4 but they failed): Commit T1\\u2013T5, then run T2 after correction.\\n- **Exception clause ambiguity** (T3's rule could read as requiring fact-checker to self-fetch): Re-run T3 with sharper exception wording; T6 re-audits.\\n- **Agent file modification** (T1\\u2013T5 accidentally touched an agent file): Roll back the offending task; T1 and T3 are most likely culprits (both edit agent-facing contracts).\\n\\nThe plan does not auto-roll-back; T6 reports and stops. Human review of the CONFLICT description determines next steps.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"\",\"issue\":\"3268\",\"tasks\":[{\"id\":\"T1\",\"title\":\"backlog-item-groomer.md: replace content-field Input with item_ref, add Step 0.0 self-fetch\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"agent\":\"dh:task-worker\",\"dependencies\":[],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[\"T3\",\"T4\",\"T5\"],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"low\",\"skills\":[],\"created\":\"2026-08-28T14:27:22.894332+00:00\",\"started\":null,\"completed\":\"2026-08-28T14:57:32.083522+00:00\",\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"`backlog-item-groomer` is the one groom-swarm teammate whose `## Input` names literal content fields (item title, item description, research questions) instead of a reference, and the file contains zero `backlog_view` calls \\u2014 even though its frontmatter `tools:` already includes `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog`. Lack of tool access is not the reason; the contract simply never asks it to fetch. This task brings it in line with `impact-analyst.md:22-24`, `classifier.md:15-20`, `alignment-analyst.md:19-21`, and `rtica-assessor.md:39-44`.\",\"objective\":\"`backlog-item-groomer.md` declares `item_ref` (plus the optional pre-computed RT-ICA summary) as its only input and fetches the item's content itself immediately before its RT-ICA pass, matching the self-fetch pattern the other groom-swarm teammates already use.\",\"requirements\":\"1. Read architect spec \\u00a71 (`artifact_read(item_id=3268, artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\")`) for the exact replacement text of both edits. Use that text; do not paraphrase it.\\n2. Replace the `## Input` section (currently lines 48-53, four literal content-field bullets) with the two-bullet `item_ref` + optional RT-ICA-summary form given in spec \\u00a71a.\\n3. Insert a new `### Step 0.0 - Fetch the Item` section immediately before the existing `### Step 0 - RT-ICA Assessment` (currently line 57), using the text in spec \\u00a71b.\\n4. Preserve the spec's timing rationale verbatim in intent: the fetch happens immediately before Step 0's RT-ICA pass, NOT earlier in the run, because the groomer always runs last and an earlier read risks grooming against an Impact Radius or RT-ICA section a peer teammate revises afterwards.\",\"constraints\":\"- Edit only `plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md`.\\n- Do not alter the file's frontmatter \\u2014 `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog` is already in `tools:`.\\n- Do not renumber, reword, or reorder the existing `Step 0`, `Step 0.5`, or any later step. The new step is additive and numbered `0.0` precisely so nothing downstream shifts.\\n- Do not remove the optional RT-ICA-summary input; it remains a legitimate pre-computed cross-agent finding, not pasted item content.\\n- Do not add tests or executable code.\",\"expected_outputs\":\"Modified: `plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md`\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"1. `## Input` lists exactly two bullets: `item_ref` and the optional RT-ICA summary. No bullet names item title, item description, or research questions as an orchestrator-supplied field.\\n2. A `### Step 0.0 - Fetch the Item` section exists immediately above `### Step 0 - RT-ICA Assessment`.\\n3. Step 0.0 contains a literal `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_view(selector=item_ref, summary=False)` call.\\n4. Step 0.0 instructs the agent not to begin from memory or assumptions, and names the sections to extract (Impact Radius, Fact-Check, Issue Classification, Root-Cause Analysis, RT-ICA, Design Intent Alignment, Research) as conditionally present.\\n5. Step 0.0 states the fetch timing rationale (fetch late, because the groomer runs last and peer sections may be revised).\\n6. `git diff --stat` lists this file and no other.\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. `grep -c 'backlog_view' plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md` returns a non-zero count (baseline was 0).\\n2. `grep -n '^## Input' -A 8 plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md` shows only the two permitted bullets.\\n3. `grep -n 'Step 0.0\\\\|Step 0 - RT-ICA' plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md` shows Step 0.0 at a lower line number than Step 0.\\n4. `git diff --name-only` lists exactly `plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md`.\\n5. Run `git add plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md` then `git commit -m \\\"fix(development-harness): make backlog-item-groomer self-fetch its item\\\"` \\u2014 no `git add .`/`-A`, no `Fixes #N` trailer.\",\"context_notes\":\"Spec \\u00a71b notes this edit also resolves feature-context Risk R6 (pasted content going stale between dispatch and use) as a side effect: self-fetch happens once, at the moment of use, instead of being frozen at dispatch time. The staleness precedent is `rtica-assessor.md:90-99`, which guards the same risk with its own late re-read.\",\"handoff\":\"Report: the final `## Input` bullets, the line number where Step 0.0 was inserted, the `backlog_view` grep count, and the commit SHA. Flag any pre-existing text elsewhere in the file that still implies the orchestrator supplies item content (T2 and T6 depend on that assumption holding).\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"medium\"},{\"id\":\"T3\",\"title\":\"subagent-contract/SKILL.md: add agent-facing <dispatch_input> self-fetch rule\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"agent\":\"dh:task-worker\",\"dependencies\":[],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[\"T1\",\"T4\",\"T5\"],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"low\",\"skills\":[],\"created\":\"2026-08-28T14:27:22.894390+00:00\",\"started\":null,\"completed\":\"2026-08-28T15:05:29.261022+00:00\",\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"`subagent-contract/SKILL.md` is the agent-facing contract: every existing section (`<status>`, `<result_destination>`, `<reporting>`) speaks in second person to the dispatched agent, and the file is loaded only via each agent's own `skills:` frontmatter. The self-fetch half of the fix \\u2014 'you have backlog access, so you fetch' \\u2014 is addressed to that audience and belongs here. The orchestrator-facing half is T4's job and must not appear in this file.\",\"objective\":\"`subagent-contract/SKILL.md` tells a dispatched agent holding `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog` to fetch the item itself rather than await pasted content, while explicitly exempting content that exists only because the current run produced it.\",\"requirements\":\"1. Read architect spec \\u00a73 for the exact `<dispatch_input>` block. Use that text verbatim.\\n2. Insert the `<dispatch_input>` section after the `</status>` close tag (line 21) and before `<result_destination>` (line 23) \\u2014 dispatch input logically precedes where output goes.\\n3. Keep the second-person voice and tag style of the surrounding sections.\\n4. Preserve the exception clause exactly: content that exists only because the current run produced it (a claim string to verify, a peer teammate's computed finding) is NOT covered by the self-fetch rule, because no `item_ref` lookup retrieves something not yet written anywhere.\",\"constraints\":\"- Edit only `plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md`.\\n- Change nothing in the existing `<status>`, `<result_destination>`, or `<reporting>` sections. This file is loaded by 28 agents in `plugins/development-harness/agents/` plus one in `python3-development`; the addition must not alter the meaning of any existing section.\\n- Add NO orchestrator-facing content here \\u2014 no rule about what an orchestrator may write, and no anti-speculation rule. `AGENTS.md:265-267` puts those in `dispatch-contract` (T4).\\n- Do not modify the file's frontmatter or its skill description.\\n- Do not add tests or executable code.\",\"expected_outputs\":\"Modified: `plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md`\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"1. A `<dispatch_input>` / `</dispatch_input>` section exists between `</status>` and `<result_destination>`.\\n2. The section is written in second person to the dispatched agent, consistent with the file's other sections.\\n3. The section conditions the rule on the agent's `tools:` list carrying `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog`.\\n4. The section contains the exception clause covering per-run-produced content.\\n5. `git diff` for this file shows only additions \\u2014 zero deletions or modifications to pre-existing lines.\\n6. Reading the new rule against `fact-checker.md:45-55` (its `CLAIM`/`SOURCE_FILE`/`PRIMARY_SOURCE`/`VERIFICATION_METHOD`/`FALSIFICATION_CRITERIA` block), a reader concludes `fact-checker` is exempt and needs no rewrite. This is the check T6 re-runs independently.\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. `grep -c 'dispatch_input' plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md` returns 2 (open + close tag).\\n2. `grep -n '^<' plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md` shows tag order: status, dispatch_input, result_destination, reporting.\\n3. `git diff --stat plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md` shows insertions only, deletions 0.\\n4. Read `plugins/development-harness/agents/fact-checker.md:45-55` and confirm the new exception clause covers it without a rewrite. If a reader could plausibly read the rule as demanding `fact-checker` self-fetch the item too, sharpen the exception clause's wording and record what changed.\\n5. Run `git add plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md` then `git commit -m \\\"fix(development-harness): add agent-facing dispatch-input self-fetch rule\\\"`.\",\"context_notes\":\"Feature-context Risk R4 is the live hazard: a rule phrased as a blanket 'agents with backlog MCP access self-fetch' would, read literally, require `fact-checker` to self-fetch an item it is not scoped to. The exception clause is the guard against that; it is load-bearing, not decoration.\\n\\nRisk R8: the measured symptom is two agents and two workflow documents. Do not widen this into an edit affecting how all 28 consumers behave beyond the additive rule itself.\",\"handoff\":\"Return: the inserted section text as it now stands in the file, the diff stat (insertions/deletions), the fact-checker exception-clause verdict from verification step 4 (and any sharpening applied), and the commit SHA.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"high\"},{\"id\":\"T4\",\"title\":\"dispatch-contract/SKILL.md: add orchestrator-facing <dispatch_prompt_scope> rule\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"agent\":\"dh:task-worker\",\"dependencies\":[],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[\"T1\",\"T3\",\"T5\"],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"low\",\"skills\":[],\"created\":\"2026-08-28T14:27:22.894424+00:00\",\"started\":\"2026-08-28T14:53:25.849103+00:00\",\"completed\":\"2026-08-28T14:59:56.787080+00:00\",\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"This file is the fifth in scope, added by spec \\u00a70 as a deliberate, cited correction to the original four-file brief. `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md:265-267` states that dispatch behaviour is defined in the `dispatch-contract` skill 'and nowhere else'. Putting an orchestrator-facing rule in the agent-facing `subagent-contract` would place it where the party who needs it never reads it (feature-context Risk R2, confirmed live in the item). `dispatch-contract` is already loaded by `implement-feature`, `multi-perspective-review`, `task-worker`, `alignment-analyst`, and `review-synthesizer`.\",\"objective\":\"`dispatch-contract/SKILL.md` states what an orchestrator may put in a dispatch prompt \\u2014 an item reference plus genuinely per-run findings, never item content pasted from its own sections \\u2014 and forbids writing a speculative conclusion or hedged verdict into a prompt for an agent whose value is independent judgement.\",\"requirements\":\"1. Read architect spec \\u00a74 for the exact `<dispatch_prompt_scope>` block. Use that text verbatim.\\n2. Add the section in the style of the file's existing `<dispatch_selection>` and `<artifact_consumption>` sections.\\n3. Keep the worked bad example verbatim \\u2014 `\\\"this is very likely `defect` \\u2014 confirm this classification yourself\\\"` is the actual text from the originating incident (feature-context \\u00a71.3). It is quoted so a reader can hold real dispatch text against the rule and reach a clear verdict; paraphrasing it defeats the purpose.\\n4. Cross-reference the agent-facing counterpart: the rule applies to an agent that can reach the item's content per that agent's `dh:subagent-contract` `<dispatch_input>` rule (T3).\",\"constraints\":\"- Edit only `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch-contract/SKILL.md`.\\n- Change nothing in the existing `<dispatch_selection>` or `<artifact_consumption>` sections.\\n- Do not restate the agent-facing self-fetch instruction here; reference it. The two halves are split by audience on purpose (spec \\u00a70 table).\\n- Do not add a mechanical guard, test, or lint rule. Feature-context Q7/R5 is explicitly deferred: the anti-speculation half is a property of prompt text generated at runtime, which no test at rest can observe.\\n- Do not modify the file's frontmatter or skill description.\",\"expected_outputs\":\"Modified: `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch-contract/SKILL.md`\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"1. A `<dispatch_prompt_scope>` / `</dispatch_prompt_scope>` section exists in the file, styled consistently with the existing tagged sections.\\n2. The section states that a dispatch prompt carries an item reference plus per-run findings no `item_ref` lookup can retrieve \\u2014 never content pasted from the item's own sections.\\n3. The section forbids speculative conclusions, pre-formed verdicts, and hedged language, naming at minimum the words 'likely', 'probably', 'seems'.\\n4. The verbatim classifier-anchoring example is present and is labelled as a violation.\\n5. The section points the reader at the agent-side `dh:subagent-contract` `<dispatch_input>` rule rathe